==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|ang|hlāf||bread}} + a second element representing {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*daigijǭ||kneader}} (compare Old English [[dǣġe]], Old English {{m|ang|dāg}} "dough"). Similar to a [[kenning]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhlæːvdiːje/|[ˈɬæːvdiːjə]|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hlǣfdīġe|f|hlǣfdīgan}}

# a [[lady]], the mistress of a household.

====Descendants====
* Middle English: {{l|enm|ladi}}, {{l|enm|laddy}}, {{l|enm|lafdi}}, {{l|enm|lavedi}}
** English: {{l|en|lady}}

